# Image Playground CLI — Project Rules

## CI/CD

- **Two workflows**: `ci.yml` (PR + push to main) and `release.yml` (tag pushes only)
- **CI runs on every PR**: build, test, and coverage report posted as PR comment
- **Swift 6.1+ required**: Swift 6.0.3 has a compiler crash bug with SwiftUI/ImagePlayground IRGen
- **Coverage**: Use `llvm-cov` for coverage reporting, post summary to PR via `sticky-pull-request-comment` action

## Code Style

- Shell scripts: `set -euo pipefail`, proper error handling, meaningful exit codes
- Swift: follow existing patterns in `app/Sources/main.swift`
- Always test changes with `--check` flag before generating images

## Release Process

1. Update VERSION in `build.sh`
2. Commit and push to main
3. Tag: `git tag -a v<X.Y.Z> -m "Release v<X.Y.Z>"`
4. Push tag: `git push origin v<X.Y.Z>`
5. CI builds the tarball and creates the GitHub release automatically

## Known Issues

- Apple Image Playground requires foreground app — the shell script handles this with `osascript` activate and process cleanup
- Mac must be unlocked and awake for image generation to work